<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <AssemblyName>eru</AssemblyName>
    <RootNamespace>Eru.Cli</RootNamespace>
    <PackageId>Eru.Tool</PackageId>
    <PackAsTool>true</PackAsTool>
    <ToolCommandName>eru</ToolCommandName>
    <Version>0.15.0</Version>
    <Authors>Devon Burriss</Authors>
    <Description>A CLI tool for sharing knowledge files across projects via git-backed sources.</Description>
    <Title>eru</Title>
    <Copyright>Copyright © 2025 Devon Burriss</Copyright>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <PackageTags>ai cli knowledge mcp dotnet-tool</PackageTags>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>Every config setting can be overridden with an environment variable that mirrors its path in the config file: `ERU__` plus the key path joined with `__` (`search.mode` is `ERU__SEARCH__MODE`, `mcp.refreshIntervalMinutes` is `ERU__MCP__REFRESHINTERVALMINUTES`), with list items indexed (`ERU__FILES__BLOCKPATTERNS__0`). The environment overrides the local and global config in the CLI, `eru browse` and `eru mcp`, so an MCP client can pass settings in its `env` block. An invalid value stops the command at startup and names the variable; `eru config get` and `eru config view` show such a value with origin `env`, and it is never written to a config file. See [environment variables](docs/reference/config-file.md#environment-variables)
Per-source settings: a `source.items` entry can carry its own `files` (`blockPatterns`, `allowPatterns`, `allowBinaries`), `search.ignorePatterns`, `okf.ignorePatterns` and `site.ignorePatterns`, which replace the global value for that source only in sync, add, read, search and the generated site. Read and write them with `eru config get|set|view --source &lt;name&gt;`, or override a configured source for one process with `ERU__SOURCE__&lt;NAME&gt;__&lt;SECTION&gt;__&lt;KEY&gt;` variables. A local entry without a `url` merges its settings key by key over the global entry's. See [per-source settings](docs/reference/config-file.md#per-source-settings)
The facet counts in the Browse sidebar now follow the filters: each count is the number of documents that match the search text and the selection in the other facets, so choosing a source narrows the tag, type and bundle counts while its own siblings keep theirs. Values with no matches are dimmed, and the File Extensions facet now shows counts too. See [facets](docs/reference/site-generation.md#layout-slots-and-widgets)
`ERU_SEARCH_MODE` is now an alias for `ERU__SEARCH__MODE`, so an invalid value is reported at startup by every command instead of only by `eru search`</PackageReleaseNotes>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/dburriss/eru</PackageProjectUrl>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/dburriss/eru</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <PublishRepositoryUrl>true</PublishRepositoryUrl>
    <EmbedUntrackedSources>true</EmbedUntrackedSources>
    <Optimize>true</Optimize>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="..\..\README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="../Eru.Domain/Eru.Domain.fsproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="../Eru.Adapters/Eru.Adapters.fsproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="../Eru.Mcp/Eru.Mcp.fsproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="../Eru.Tui/Eru.Tui.fsproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="../Eru.Site/Eru.Site.fsproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="../Eru.Serve/Eru.Serve.fsproj" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Argu" Version="6.*" />
    <PackageReference Include="Spectre.Console" Version="0.*" />
  </ItemGroup>
